 This install applies to "Secret Weapons of the Luftwaffe" 2.2, an unofficial
 Amiga port of the 1991 PC game by Lucasfilm Games and Totally Games.


 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad version 17.0 or better and a PAL or NTSC
 Amiga with AGA and a 68020 or better. The installed program uses 2 MB
 ChipMem and 6.5 MB OtherMem, including its Kickstart image; 8 MB Fast RAM
 is enough. With 8 MB, PreLoad can hold only part of the game files and the
 screen blanks briefly while the rest load; about 12 MB Fast RAM preloads
 them all. Flight is slow on a 68020; a 68030 or better is recommended. The
 data cache needs the MMU: WHDLoad uses it on a 68040 or 68060, on a 68030
 only with the WHDLoad option MMU (add the tooltype MMU to the icon).

 The game requires an installed A600/A1200/A4000 Kickstart 3.1 image.
 The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts" and
 must be named "kick40063.A600", "kick40068.A1200" or "kick40068.A4000".
 Additionally the file "kick40063.A600.RTB", "kick40068.A1200.RTB" or
 "kick40068.A4000.RTB" must be installed in the same directory as the kickstart
 image. It can be found in the archive "util/boot/skick346.lha" on aminet.


 Installation:
 -------------
 The install does not include the original game files. It installs them from
 the three 1.44 MB PC floppies of "Air Combat Classics" (LucasArts, 1993),
 which hold version 2.2. Other releases are not supported. Run the Install
 icon and select a drawer containing either the disk images

   Disk1.img  Disk2.img  Disk3.img

 or the files CLASSICS.001, CLASSICS.002 and CLASSICS.003 copied from the
 disks. Every file is checked; damaged or other disks are refused.

 The disk images are not provided here. They are available, for example, in
 the "The Good Old Days" floppy image collection (ID 496).

 Optionally, the game can use the sampled sound effects of the Amiga version
 of "Their Finest Hour". Choose Their Finest Hour sound effects and select the
 file sfx.rsc in your Their Finest Hour installation, for example
 TheirFinestHour/data/sfx.rsc. The Custom1 tooltype switches between the
 sound effects later: 1 for Their Finest Hour, 0 for the original AdLib.

 To update, select the same parent drawer and choose Keep. Use existing (the
 default) keeps the installed game files; Replace installs them again from the
 disks. Pilots, films and missions are kept either way.


 Playing:
 --------
 Keyboard and mouse work as in the PC original; keys are at their US
 keyboard positions. See the original manual for the controls. Quit from the
 game's menus. The WHDLoad QuitKey (Help) quits immediately.


